+{"id":"CF-198","title":"P4 — docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md still claims its mapping table names every numbered section, but it ends at §37 while the tree has §38, and the prose arm count still says 40","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-04 at published tip 2156061 (clone of origin/main, clean porcelain). b626238 (CF-182 gate) appended §38 to `tests/selftest.sh` (`say \"38. the milestone blocker list resolves every cited id in one namespace (CF-182)\"` at :1866, +50 lines). The docs lane's follow-up 933c1fb (\"docs(plan): re-measure the acceptance-plan census for §38\") corrected only the FIRST number: `docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md:5` now reads 38 sections. The rest of the same paragraph set is still pre-§38:\n\n- `docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md:104` still says \"the mapping below names every numbered section in the current tree — 37, plus three lettered arms (§4b, §7b, §31b), so 40 arms\" — the tree has 38 numbered sections, so the total is 41 arms and the cited 37 is one short.\n- The mapping table still ends at `§37` (:143); §38 has no row anywhere in the table, so the sentence that promises to name every numbered section is false as written.\n- The repo's own census (`docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh`) reports the mismatch beside the corrected prose: probe prints `selftest_sections=38`, `plan_says=38`, `mapping_last=37`, `DRIFT: ... mapping table ends at section 37`.\n\nThis is the residual of a partial fix, not a re-filing of the original count defect: after 933c1fb the headline number is right, which makes the missing §38 row harder to notice rather than caught.\n\nDistinct from CF-113 (pending — the census cannot SEE lettered sub-arms), CF-186 (pending — the §7c census GATE was deleted by 4ce1e48; that row owns restoring the gate) and CF-155 (complete — the earlier 29→30 instance at 32f38a5). This row owns the mapping table and arm-count claim, which a fix that only edits the headline number leaves stale.","acceptance_criteria":"AC0 — reproduce at the filing tip from the repository root: the `probe` field prints `selftest_sections=38`, `plan_says=38`, `mapping_last=37` and the `DRIFT:` line, exit 0. Re-derive at your own tip; those numbers are today's measurement, not a frozen expectation of the fix.\n\nAC1 — at the landing commit `docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md` names every numbered section the tree has: the mapping table carries one row per `^say \"N.` section, and the arm count in the prose equals the derived total (numbered sections + lettered arms), both sides DERIVED by a committed checker rather than hand-typed, so the next section that lands cannot leave the table or the count behind.\n\nAC2 — the check can fail: a named arm in `tests/selftest.sh` runs the checker over a fixture (a copy of the plan with one section row removed, or a fixture selftest carrying one extra section) and must print a NAMED FAIL row naming the section number and the side that lacks it, exiting non-zero there, while the same run over the real tree stays green. Quote the fixture output — do not assert the substring FAIL alone.\n\nAC3 — `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS`, `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK`, and the landing is pushed with `git rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD` = 0.","probe":"c=$(grep -cE '^say \"[0-9]+\\.' tests/selftest.sh); m=$(grep -oE '^\\| §[0-9]+' docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md | grep -oE '[0-9]+' | sort -n | tail -1); s=$(grep -oE 'carries [0-9]+ sections' docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md | head -1 | grep -oE '[0-9]+'); echo \"selftest_sections=$c\"; echo \"plan_says=$s\"; echo \"mapping_last=$m\"; if [ \"$c\" = \"$s\" ] && [ \"$c\" = \"$m\" ]; then echo \"OK pins agree\"; else echo \"DRIFT: selftest has $c sections, plan claims $s, mapping table ends at section $m\"; fi; exit 0","created_at":"2026-11-04T10:15:57Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T10:15:57Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"3e117d47d6dfae89f57b4b218fd6a10f3751ee1dff4acda7398dcfe738117e1c"}}
